content='```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml file\n  ansible.builtin.include_tasks:\n    file: assert.yml\n  delegate_to: localhost\n  run_once: true\n\n- name: Install prerequisites\n  ansible.builtin.package:\n    name: "{{ vault_prerequisites }}"\n    state: present\n\n- name: Include installation method specific tasks\n  ansible.builtin.include_tasks:\n    file: "{{ vault_installation_method }}.yml"\n\n- name: Add Vault environment variables\n  ansible.builtin.lineinfile:\n    path: /etc/vault.d/vault.env\n    line: "{{ item.key }}={{ item.value }}"\n    create: yes\n  loop: "{{ vault_environment_settings | dict2items }}"\n  notify: restart vault\n\n- name: Include hardening tasks\n  ansible.builtin.include_tasks:\n    file: hardening.yml\n\n- name: Start and enable vault on OSS\n  ansible.builtin.service:\n    name: vault\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n  when: vault_type == "oss"\n\n- name: Enable vault (non-OSS)\n  ansible.builtin.service:\n    name: vault\n    enabled: yes\n  when: vault_type != "oss"\n\nhandlers:\n  - name: restart vault\n    ansible.builtin.service:\n      name: vault\n      state: restarted\n```\n\nThis playbook is structured to be included in an Ansible Role under the `tasks/main.yml` file. Each task is defined according to the provided descriptions, ensuring the correct order and module usage. Handlers are used to restart the vault service when environment variables are updated.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'phi4:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-13T21:04:16.147547512Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 5379975623, 'load_duration': 63448355, 'prompt_eval_count': 485, 'prompt_eval_duration': 51635879, 'eval_count': 330, 'eval_duration': 5264009344, 'model_name': 'phi4:14b'} id='run--e742a0e8-b62d-4a38-8cec-44a58e26864d-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 485, 'output_tokens': 330, 'total_tokens': 815}
